00079E50                            ; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
00079E50                            ; Unused RAM addresses for FM and PSG channel variables used by the Special SFX
00079E50                            ; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
00079E50                            ; The first block would have been used for overriding the music tracks
00079E50                            ; as they have a lower priority, just as they are in Sound_PlaySFX
00079E50                            ; The third block would be used to set up the Special SFX
00079E50                            ; The second block, however, is for the SFX tracks, which have a higher priority
00079E50                            ; and would be checked for if they're currently playing
00079E50                            ; If they are, then the third block would be used again, this time to mark
00079E50                            ; the new tracks as 'currently playing'
00079E50                            
00079E50                            ; These were actually used in Moonwalker's driver (and other SMPS 68k Type 1a drivers)
00079E50                            
00079E50                            ; BGMFM4PSG3RAM:
00079E50                            ;SpecSFX_BGMChannelRAM:
